---
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site collects, what it doesn't, and how third-party affiliate tracking works."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Short version: no accounts, no personal data collected, nothing sold. Affiliate links and analytics involve third parties, and that's spelled out below.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>
    This is a static site. There are no accounts, no comments, and no forms. <strong>The site itself collects nothing that identifies you.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    The host (Cloudflare) keeps standard server logs for security and operations, which can include IP address, browser type, and request time. Those logs belong to the host; I only see aggregate figures.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses cookie-free analytics that do not track you across sites. It records page views, referring domain, and approximate region. <strong>No tracking cookies, no profiles, no cross-site tracking.</strong>
  </p>
  <p class="meta">
    <!-- WARNING: the paragraph above describes Cloudflare Web Analytics /
         Plausible / Umami. If you switch to Google Analytics you MUST rewrite
         it — GA sets cookies, tracks across sites, and needs a consent banner
         in GDPR regions. Do not leave this paragraph unchanged. -->
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links and third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site carries affiliate links. When you click one, <strong>the destination merchant or affiliate network may set a cookie in your browser</strong> so that a later purchase can be attributed here and a commission paid to me.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those cookies are set and read by third parties. This site can't see inside them and can't delete them on your behalf. You can:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>block third-party cookies in your browser settings;</li>
    <li>visit the merchant in a private window;</li>
    <li>skip the link entirely and search for the merchant by name — the price is identical.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The full explanation is in the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    This site links out to third-party websites. Once you leave, their privacy policies apply; I'm not responsible for their content or how they handle data.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because this site stores no personal data about you, there's usually nothing to access, correct, or delete. If you believe it holds information about you in some way, <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>email me</a> and I'll check and deal with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    The date below changes when this policy does. Anything that materially changes how data is handled will also be noted on the home page.
  </p>

  <p class="meta">Last updated: September 2026</p>
</Base>
